# Flutter Testing Rules

- Every critical user workflow must have automated coverage at the appropriate level.
- Unit-test state/application logic and sync conflict logic.
- Widget-test important screens and state transitions.
- Integration-test authentication, delivery lifecycle, offline persistence, synchronization, location permissions, and proof-of-delivery workflows where feasible.
- Test duplicate sync events and app restart during pending synchronization.
- Test authorization-driven UI behavior but do not treat UI tests as server authorization validation.
- Use fakes/mocks for remote providers and map/payment/notification services.
- Add regression tests for every production bug in critical paths.
